        "link": "https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260429-russia-scales-down-ww2-victory-parade-due-to-ukrainian-threat",
        "orario": "23:23 - 29 Aprile",
        "timestamp": 1777497839,
        "contenuto_esteso": "To display this content from YouTube, you must enable advertisement tracking and audience measurement. One of your browser extensions seems to be blocking the video player from loading. To watch this content, you may need to disable it on this site. Russia scales down WW2 victory parade due to Ukrainian threat Issued on: 29/04/2026 - 23:23 No military hardware will roll through Red Square in Russia's grand World War II victory parade next month -- a precautionary measure given the threat of Ukrainian retaliatory strikes, the Kremlin said Wednesday. The move to a slimmed-down May 9 parade -- typically a bombastic display of Russia's military might -- comes more than four years into Russia's war in Ukraine that has killed hundreds of thousands and drained vast economic resources. Assad regime trials are 'integral for Syria to move on' from civil war, atrocities 29/04/2026 Middle East Israeli maps outline expanded zone of military control in Gaza 29/04/2026 Middle East Mali faces 'very high risk' of new coup d'état, analyst says, amid jihadist insurgence 29/04/2026 Africa Viral LEGO-style AI videos blur line between entertainment and propaganda 29/04/2026 Middle East Foreign minister signals new era for Armenia: Peace, EU ambitions, trade, 'huge' infrastructure plan 29/04/2026 Asia / Pacific Putin, in call with Trump, put forward ideas on Iran, Kremlin says 29/04/2026 Americas Tuareg rebels urge Russian forces to leave Mali 29/04/2026 Africa London police say stabbing of 2 Jewish men is declared a terrorist incident 29/04/2026 Genius & Gadgets: Discovering Paris’s annual invention competition 29/04/2026"
